From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntoskrnl.exe, hal: IRQL, probes, MmCopyVirtualMemory, contiguous memory and MDL pages (3744)

ntoskrnl.exe, hal: IRQL, probes, MmCopyVirtualMemory, contiguous memory and MDL pages

A driver's thread now has an IRQL: KfRaiseIrql (one argument on x64 as in
Windows), KeLowerIrql, KeRaiseIrqlToDpcLevel, KeGetCurrentIrql, and the spin
locks raise to DISPATCH_LEVEL and restore the old level. ProbeForRead and
ProbeForWrite raise the documented exceptions, KeQueryPriorityThread gives
the dynamic priority, MmCopyVirtualMemory copies between processes,
MmAllocateContiguousMemory and MmAllocatePagesForMdl hand out pages with
identity page numbers. The wdm.h declarations and PFN_NUMBER (pointer sized)
follow.

Rebased at integration (integ-2026-10) onto stubs-6 5052-5093 (K-MM): MmBuildMdlForNonPagedPool, MmMapLockedPagesSpecifyCache, MmUnmapLockedPages, ProbeForRead and ProbeForWrite were implemented by stubs-6 and 3744; stubs-6's versions (with their mutants) kept, 3744's dropped; 3744 keeps IRQL, MmCopyVirtualMemory (with its probe_user_range), contiguous memory, MmAllocatePagesForMdl, KeQueryPriorityThread and the wdm.h changes.
